## Doc–MLIR pipeline (documentation discipline)

- When **creating or editing** documentation in this repo (specs, ADR, ideas, SDLC docs), use **KG-first** as canonical format for each logical chunk (section, paragraph, requirement list).
- **KG-first**: in KG store only concepts, relations, effects (no phrases). Per chunk: **SPARQL query** (structural, no CONTAINS on phrases); optionally KG facts (Turtle); **MLIR layers** `ttl.sdlc_kg` and `ttl.sdlc_doc_intent` (or project-equivalent prefixes). Text is generated only by LLM from final MLIR.
- **Optional/deprecated**: MLIR footnote format `<!-- mlir: path/to/file.mlir [#anchor] dialect=ttl.sdlc_doc -->` — use only for legacy; prefer KG-first.
- Follow the canonical pipeline: **docs/sdlc/00_Main/02_Architecture/00_Doc_MLIR_GraphDB_Pipeline.md** (§3, §3.2 contract, §4 example).
- Register dialects and transformations: **in-repo SoT** is **`.cursor/artifacts_mlir_graphdb`** (mlir/, graphdb/). Optionally `docs/sdlc/_KG_MLIR` in portfolio/cursorrules when present; when absent, use `.cursor/artifacts_mlir_graphdb` only.

